This is a post-publish fixup audit. The deterministic part of the
harness has already:

- Force-pushed `{{ release_branch }}` onto a fresh snapshot of
  `{{ base_branch }}` (no preserved commits beyond the new release
  commit).
- Folded any new `## Unreleased` subsections (post `{{ fixup_tag }}`
  drift) into the shipped v{{ target_version }} body in CHANGELOG.md.
- Skipped the audit, the publish dry-run, and the tag step — the
  release was already published.

Do one bounded evidence pass to confirm the fold is sane. Suggested
inspections:

- `release_read CHANGELOG.md` — confirm the v{{ target_version }}
  section reads as a coherent set of behavior changes for that
  version after the fold.
- `release_run` with `git log --oneline {{ fixup_tag }}..origin/{{ base_branch }}` —
  see exactly what landed on `{{ base_branch }}` since the original
  publish so you can judge whether each new Unreleased entry actually
  belongs in `{{ target_version }}`.
- `release_search` on a representative folded entry to confirm it
  describes behavior shipped in the original tag.

Return one short Audit block when finalization arrives. Do not produce
a draft changelog.
